; Facts that no statement shows: a property's purchase price and value, a loan before the first
; statement, a closed fund, money lent to a person, an account without statements (a meal card, a
; pension fund, building savings), a tax accrued in the year of the income. Statements and rules book
; the payments; this file adds what they cannot.
; `pad` + `balance` set an account to a known value and book the difference to the other account.
; The examples use made-up values.

; 2010-01-01 * "Flat" "Purchase price"
;   Assets:Me:Property:Flat  100000.00 EUR
;   Equity:Opening-Balances
;
; A mortgage that started before the first statement and was paid off by a later loan:
; 2010-01-01 pad Liabilities:Bank:Mortgage Equity:Opening-Balances
; 2015-06-01 balance Liabilities:Bank:Mortgage  0.00 EUR
;
; An assessed value above the cost is a revaluation, not income (open Equity:Revaluation):
; 2015-05-31 pad Assets:Me:Property:Flat Equity:Revaluation
; 2015-06-01 balance Assets:Me:Property:Flat  150000.00 EUR
;
; A tax paid later, accrued in the year of the income (a rule books the payment to the liability):
; 2025-12-31 * "Income tax accrued for 2025"
;   Expenses:Taxes:Income  1500.00 EUR
;   Liabilities:Taxes:Income
;
; A closed fund: what the payouts exceed the deposits by is the gain:
; 2018-12-31 pad Assets:Me:Investments:Fund Income:Investments:Gains
; 2019-01-01 balance Assets:Me:Investments:Fund  0.00 EUR
